---
import BaseHead from '../components/BaseHead.astro';
import Header from '../components/Header.astro';
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';
---

<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
	<head>
		<BaseHead
			title="EverThawe | Oh KAY Gamers"
			description="Door to the EverThawe — an interactive story set in the world of Neridia. A hybrid book-and-game from Oh KAY Gamers."
		/>
	</head>
	<body>
		<Header />
		<main class="everthawe-page">

			<!-- ── HERO ── -->
			<section class="hero">
				<div class="hero-inner">
					<p class="brand">Oh KAY Writers</p>
					<p class="eyebrow">Neridia</p>
					<h1>Door to the <span class="title-accent">EverThawe</span></h1>
					<p class="tagline">
						A hybrid book and game within the world of Neridia — read the
						book, explore a part of the world, uncover secrets.
					</p>
					<div class="hero-divider">
						<span>◆</span>
					</div>
				</div>
			</section>

			<!-- ── WHAT IS IT ── -->
			<section class="section">
				<div class="section-label">
					<span class="label-icon">⬡</span> Interactive Novel
				</div>

				<div class="card">
					<p class="dropcap">
						Door to the EverThawe is something that I have been quietly
						building alongside Paranoia and Shadow Guardian. This project
						doesn't fit within the horror catalogue, so it gets its own
						home here.
					</p>
					<p>
						It is built like a book first and a game second, as most of
						your time will be spent reading (or listening to the audio
						book). But you can spend time exploring the world, unlocking
						artworks, browsing the wiki and maps. You pick up the next
						book and unlock more from the map, more lore, and artwork.
					</p>
					<p>
						It is going to be played in portrait orientation on the phone,
						or normally via the PC. It's a book within the world. Or that
						is the theme I am going for.
					</p>
				</div>
			</section>

			<!-- ── ROADMAP ── -->
			<section class="section">
				<div class="section-label">
					<span class="label-icon">◆</span> Roadmap
				</div>

				<div class="card">
					<p>
						Currently three books (novellas) are already written and in
						the editing process. My goal is to get a demo of how the
						game/book is going to look — and make it available for you
						to enjoy along with the first book, for free. You will be
						able to download it via the Google Play Store, or access
						it via the web — links will be provided.
					</p>
				</div>
			</section>

			<!-- ── STATUS & PLATFORMS ── -->
			<section class="section">
				<div class="section-label">
					<span class="label-icon">◎</span> Where You'll Play It
				</div>

				<div class="status-grid">
					<div class="card status-card">
						<div class="badge-row">
							<span class="badge badge-dev">In Development</span>
						</div>
						<h3>Status</h3>
						<p>
							Currently in active development. No release date yet — this
							one is being built slowly, the way a book gets written. Follow
							the dev blog for updates.
						</p>
					</div>

					<div class="card status-card">
						<div class="badge-row">
							<span class="badge badge-platform">PC</span>
							<span class="badge badge-platform">Android</span>
							<span class="badge badge-platform badge-soon">WebGL · Soon</span>
						</div>
						<h3>Platforms</h3>
						<p>
							Built in Unity for Windows and Android first. A free WebGL
							demo will land on itch.io once the first vertical slice is
							ready to share.
						</p>
					</div>
				</div>
			</section>

			<!-- ── COMMON QUESTIONS ── -->
			<section class="section">
				<div class="section-label">
					<span class="label-icon">✦</span> Common Questions
				</div>

				<div class="faq-list">
					<div class="card">
						<h3>Will there be ads on the app?</h3>
						<p>
							At the moment — absolutely not. It breaks the immersion.
							There might be changes in the future, but I want to make
							sure the ads will never interfere with the experience. But
							there will be in-app purchases as more books become
							available to read.
						</p>
						<p>
							My hope is to also get the books available on Steam —
							where you will be able to buy more books in the form
							of DLCs.
						</p>
					</div>

					<div class="card">
						<h3>Can I support the project?</h3>
						<p>
							Yes! I have a Ko-Fi, and this will certainly help speed
							up my journey. Once the demo is complete, there may be
							other ways for you to support the project and receive
							rewards within the book/game as well.
						</p>
						<div class="btn-row">
							<a
								href="https://ko-fi.com/kay1o1"
								target="_blank"
								rel="noopener noreferrer"
								class="btn btn-primary"
							>
								Support on Ko-Fi →
							</a>
						</div>
					</div>
				</div>
			</section>

			<!-- ── FOLLOW ── -->
			<section class="section follow-section">
				<div class="follow-inner">
					<p class="eyebrow">Stay With It</p>
					<h2>Follow the Build</h2>
					<p class="follow-body">
						EverThawe is going to take a while. If you want to watch a
						book-game grow from a dock and a door into something bigger,
						the dev blog is where it happens.
					</p>
					<a href="/blog" class="btn btn-primary">Read the Dev Blog →</a>
				</div>
			</section>

		</main>
		<Footer />
	</body>
</html>

<style>
	.everthawe-page {
		width: 900px;
		max-width: calc(100% - 2em);
		margin: auto;
		padding: 0 1em 5em;
	}

	/* ── Hero ── */
	.hero {
		text-align: center;
		padding: 5em 1em 3.5em;
		border-bottom: 1px solid rgba(139,0,0,0.18);
		margin-bottom: 3em;
		position: relative;
	}

	.hero-inner {
		max-width: 640px;
		margin: 0 auto;
	}

	.brand {
		font-family: 'Cinzel', Georgia, serif;
		font-size: 1.4em;
		font-weight: 700;
		letter-spacing: 0.18em;
		text-transform: uppercase;
		color: var(--accent);
		text-shadow: 0 0 18px rgba(139,0,0,0.55), 0 0 4px rgba(255,255,255,0.15);
		margin: 0 0 0.5em;
	}

	.eyebrow {
		font-family: 'Cinzel', Georgia, serif;
		font-size: 0.78em;
		letter-spacing: 0.22em;
		text-transform: uppercase;
		color: var(--accent);
		margin: 0 0 0.8em;
	}

	.hero h1 {
		font-size: 3.6em;
		margin: 0 0 0.5em;
		line-height: 1.1;
		text-shadow: 0 0 50px rgba(139,0,0,0.25);
	}

	.title-accent {
		color: var(--accent);
		font-style: italic;
	}

	.tagline {
		font-size: 1.1em;
		color: var(--gray-text);
		line-height: 1.7;
		font-family: 'Crimson Text', Georgia, serif;
		font-style: italic;
		max-width: 540px;
		margin: 0 auto 1.6em;
	}

	.hero-divider {
		margin-top: 1.6em;
		color: var(--accent);
		font-size: 1.4em;
		opacity: 0.6;
		letter-spacing: 0.8em;
		padding-left: 0.8em;
	}

	/* ── Section ── */
	.section {
		margin-bottom: 4em;
	}

	.section-label {
		display: flex;
		align-items: center;
		gap: 0.55em;
		font-family: 'Cinzel', Georgia, serif;
		font-size: 0.7em;
		letter-spacing: 0.2em;
		text-transform: uppercase;
		color: var(--accent);
		margin-bottom: 1.2em;
		padding-bottom: 0.6em;
		border-bottom: 1px solid rgba(139,0,0,0.15);
	}

	.label-icon {
		font-size: 1.1em;
		opacity: 0.7;
	}

	/* ── Cards ── */
	.card {
		background: var(--bg-card);
		border: 1px solid rgba(139,0,0,0.2);
		border-radius: 10px;
		padding: 2em 2.4em;
		transition: border-color 0.25s, box-shadow 0.25s;
	}

	.card:hover {
		border-color: rgba(139,0,0,0.4);
		box-shadow: 0 4px 24px rgba(139,0,0,0.1);
	}

	.card h2 {
		font-size: 1.8em;
		margin: 0 0 0.6em;
	}

	.card h3 {
		font-size: 1.3em;
		margin: 0.5em 0 0.6em;
	}

	.card p {
		font-size: 1.02em;
		line-height: 1.8;
		color: var(--gray-text);
		margin: 0 0 1em;
	}

	.card p:last-child {
		margin-bottom: 0;
	}

	/* ── FAQ List ── */
	.faq-list {
		display: flex;
		flex-direction: column;
		gap: 1.2em;
	}

	.faq-list .card h3 {
		color: var(--accent);
		font-size: 1.25em;
		margin-top: 0;
	}

	/* ── Status Grid ── */
	.status-grid {
		display: grid;
		grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(280px, 1fr));
		gap: 1.5em;
	}

	.status-card p {
		font-size: 0.95em;
	}

	/* ── Badges ── */
	.badge-row {
		display: flex;
		flex-wrap: wrap;
		gap: 0.5em;
		margin-bottom: 0.5em;
	}

	.badge {
		display: inline-flex;
		align-items: center;
		gap: 0.35em;
		font-size: 0.7em;
		font-family: 'Cinzel', Georgia, serif;
		letter-spacing: 0.08em;
		text-transform: uppercase;
		padding: 0.25em 0.7em;
		border-radius: 4px;
		font-weight: 700;
	}

	.badge-dev      { background: rgba(234,179,8,0.12); color: #fbbf24; border: 1px solid rgba(234,179,8,0.25); }
	.badge-platform { background: rgba(139,0,0,0.15); color: #e87070; border: 1px solid rgba(139,0,0,0.3); }
	.badge-soon     { background: transparent; color: var(--gray-text); border: 1px dashed rgba(139,0,0,0.3); opacity: 0.85; }

	/* ── Follow Section ── */
	.follow-section {
		margin-top: 2em;
	}

	.follow-inner {
		text-align: center;
		padding: 3.2em 2em;
		background: linear-gradient(135deg, rgba(139,0,0,0.06) 0%, transparent 60%);
		border: 1px solid rgba(139,0,0,0.15);
		border-radius: 12px;
	}

	.follow-inner h2 {
		font-size: 2em;
		margin: 0.3em 0 0.7em;
	}

	.follow-body {
		max-width: 500px;
		margin: 0 auto 1.8em;
		font-size: 1em;
		line-height: 1.75;
		color: var(--gray-text);
	}

	/* ── Buttons ── */
	.btn-row {
		display: flex;
		flex-wrap: wrap;
		gap: 0.8em;
		margin-top: 0.4em;
	}

	.btn {
		display: inline-flex;
		align-items: center;
		gap: 0.5em;
		padding: 0.7em 1.6em;
		border-radius: 6px;
		font-family: 'Cinzel', Georgia, serif;
		font-size: 0.8em;
		font-weight: 700;
		letter-spacing: 0.08em;
		text-decoration: none;
		transition: all 0.2s;
	}

	.btn-primary {
		background: var(--accent);
		color: var(--white);
		border: 1px solid rgba(185,28,28,0.6);
	}
	.btn-primary:hover {
		background: var(--accent-bright);
		color: var(--white);
		box-shadow: 0 0 18px rgba(139,0,0,0.5);
		text-shadow: none;
	}

	/* ── Responsive ── */
	@media (max-width: 600px) {
		.hero h1 { font-size: 2.5em; }
		.card { padding: 1.6em 1.4em; }
		.card h2 { font-size: 1.5em; }
		.status-grid { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
	}
</style>
